WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.830
- On Clubhouse, I feel
like I could really be

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:05.560
all aspects of who I am, so I've hosted

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.380
parenting rooms, I've hosted Latino rooms,

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.820
I've hosted a gay room for LGBT people.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.610
- Clubhouse is for comedy impressions.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.680
You could be listening in, and one moment

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.920
I might be John Oliver, the
host of Last Week Tonight.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.950
Then you become Jeff Goldblum.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.810
Ah hello, yes, yes, Daddy
Jeff Goldblum, listen folks.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.950
- Clubhouse is for everyone to get

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.690
a little bit of podcast, a little bit

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.020
of conference, a little bit of Twitter,

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.770
and a little bit of radio all in one.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:41.140
- Clubhouse everyone, this is it.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.650
The new audio only social media thing

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.783
that everyone is talking about.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.640
But even though this is
very much about audio,

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.110
I'm coming to you in video to make

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.200
this a little bit easier to understand.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.240
Clubhouse is very much not about video.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.820
There's no video over here either

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:02.150
in Twitter's Clubhouse
clone, Twitter Spaces.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:05.070
Both of these are very much about talking,

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.740
a lot of talking and listening.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.370
So that's exactly what I did,
I went inside these apps,

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.160
well, literally right
now, to talk and listen

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.630
to the people experimenting
with this stuff

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:19.020
and to find out if this is all a big deal

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:22.290
or just another passing social media fad.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.991
So let's start with
what this is all about.

00:01:24.991 --> 00:01:27.020
(rapid clicking)

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.440
- Clubhouse is a platform that facilitates

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.800
real-time audio rooms that enable both

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.370
listening like passive listening,

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.900
but also engagement from the audience.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.250
- That's Alexis Gay.

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.380
She's a comedian, a podcaster,

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.220
and an early adopter of Clubhouse

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.760
who's amassed over a million followers.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.390
The best way to think of this app is like

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:51.320
a big hallway full of different
rooms with virtual stages.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.350
Walk down, OK fine,
scroll down this hallway

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.810
and you see all the open rooms.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:58.990
They're recommended
based on who you follow

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:01.630
and what topics you tell the
app you're interested in.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:03.850
Join one and you automatically pop up

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:05.770
and start hearing what's going on inside.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.690
You can also make a room of your own.

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.330
You can just invite a few
people, or open the door

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.250
to everyone, which is
what I did with Alexis.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.380
Before I knew it, there were
over 1,000 people in our room.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.190
Usually there are only a handful.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:20.800
I even spotted media
personality Perez Hilton

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.410
in the audience and
brought him up on stage.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:27.030
I think this is like the real
Perez Hilton, I'm not sure.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.743
- [Narrator] Oh yeah,
it's definitely Perez.

00:02:28.743 --> 00:02:29.917
- Yeah.

00:02:29.917 --> 00:02:31.740
Oh, he just raised his hand,
should we bring him up?

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:33.230
The person who controls the room

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.220
can bring others up to talk.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.430
When you talk, the ring around
your profile photo blinks

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.960
and you can mute and unmute your mic here.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.630
Everyone else is just
a listener in the room.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:47.070
You can tap the hand icon
to speak or ask a question.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:50.260
When the event is over, it's
over, there's no recording.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:51.760
In fact, you get this big warning

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.570
when you start screen recording.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:56.870
I got permission to record all
the speakers for this video.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:01.110
Twitter Spaces work similarly,
and looks really similar too.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.300
Though Twitter went with the circle icon

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.330
versus the squirkle of Clubhouse.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:08.260
So yeah, it's totally, totally different.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.760
This purple circle here
indicates that there's a space

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.930
going on right now that you can join.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.240
Clubhouse, for the time being,

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.960
is iPhone only, and invite only.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.970
Twitter Spaces is in testing and will

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:20.650
roll out to more people soon.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:23.770
So that's the app, but what's
there to actually listen to?

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:27.650
Well, everything and also kind of nothing.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:29.550
There's a lot of rooms about business.

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:32.200
The social media business,
the tech business,

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.580
the entertainment business, the business

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:38.750
of business, oh, and so much crypto.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:42.850
- We use Clubhouse to
spread Bitcoin education

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:45.970
and knowledge and connect
with people new to Bitcoin,

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.620
and people who've been in
the space for a long time.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.870
- [Joanna] Corey Klippsten,
the CEO of swanbitcoin.com

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.520
runs the Bitcoin Cafe, a
group that has multiple rooms

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:59.120
that run Monday through
Friday, 20 hours per day.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.010
- [Corey] In the short
term, affecting the market

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:03.680
and going in the direction
of the US dollar crashing

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.430
and Bitcoin, you know, taking over.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.630
- And if the crypto talk doesn't

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:09.390
put you to sleep, there are lullabies.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:12.260
- And so I just got on Clubhouse

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:13.350
and I was like, you know what?

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.304
I'm just going to start
playing lullabies again.

00:04:16.304 --> 00:04:21.304
♪ Maybe slow things down ♪

00:04:21.871 --> 00:04:25.704
♪ If I could find father time ♪

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.730
- Every night at 9:00
pm, people show up to

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:34.490
a lullaby club where
Axel Mansoor performs.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:37.500
Clubhouse, which periodically
changes its app icon to

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.204
a different user just changed
the icon to a photo of Axel.

00:04:41.204 --> 00:04:42.600
(rapid clicking)

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:47.130
But why not video, and why
audio, and why right now?

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:50.150
Well, partially COVID-19 and Zoom fatigue.

00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:51.980
Matthew Friend, a comedian who's gotten

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:54.680
really into the app
summed it up perfectly.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.940
- Kind of like how back
in the '50s with radio

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:59.050
when you could kind of
listen to baseball games

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:00.710
and that was your only way of seeing it.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.760
It's kind of like that
now where you're sort of

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.140
able to just listen and imagine.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:06.900
- And that brings me to the
biggest question I've had

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:10.160
through this whole thing,
is this just a passing fad?

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.690
Are we going to really want to do this

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:14.080
when we can go back to real live events

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.660
and comedy shows and music events

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:20.410
and all of the things
we used to do in person?

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:22.040
Twitter's betting that's not the case

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:24.340
and says it's more than a Clubhouse clone.

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:26.860
Dantley Davis, Twitter's
Chief Design Officer,

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:29.180
told me about it during
a Google Meet call.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.660
We couldn't use Spaces just yet for this.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:35.220
- To set the record straight, we actually

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:39.960
started thinking about Spaces in 2019

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:42.300
and as we were getting ready to ship

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.600
the group version of
Voices, which is Spaces

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.610
as you see it now,
Clubhouse came to market.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.770
So Clubhouse gave us validation

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:52.485
that other people were
thinking about this as well.

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:53.810
(rapid clicking)

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.550
- After spending time in both of these,

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:57.640
I think social audio is here to stay,

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:59.640
at least in some shape or form.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:04.640
But with it brings old and new
issues, privacy is a big one.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.880
Clubhouse, for instance,
is very aggressive

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.720
about uploading your
contacts to its servers.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.770
The company says users
will soon be able to

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:15.050
use the app to delete
contacts from its servers.

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.680
And then there's moderation,
it's harder to moderate

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:20.913
hate speech and misinformation
in real-time audio.

00:06:21.798 --> 00:06:23.410
But I'm going to go
with Perez on this one.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:26.040
- Because I may be an old fart,

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.110
I'm going to turn 43 next month,

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:31.630
but unlike some of my peers, or friends,

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:35.690
when something new is popping,
I get excited about it.

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:38.250
I don't roll my eyes and groan like ugh,

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:41.510
another app that I've got to try.

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:44.530
No, I'll try it out and
see what it's all about.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:46.250
- Plus, unlike me for this video

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:48.130
you don't need to do
your hair or your makeup

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.410
or get some fancy Zoom
background to participate

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:55.833
in this next wave of
social media, fun or chaos.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.340
Yeah, it's already pretty much chaos.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.460
- I just got to say that when you

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:03.530
do the Howard Stern, it gets so crazy

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:05.120
because you get so deep and people

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:07.713
are very confused if
it's actually him or not.

